  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>If&nbsp;the apparent dip circle is at an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;with true dip circle then,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/11ac7fc1-12b6-4947-bd46-b6fc87302962-D780.png\" style=\"width: 284px; height: 401px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>'</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mfenced><mi>&#981;</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>'</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, apparent dip angle is greater than true dip angle.</p><p>Hence, true dip <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is less than apparent dip&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msup><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mfenced></math></p>",
